.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/path-exists Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "path-exists [![Build Status](https://travis-ci.org/sindresorhus/path-exists.svg?branch=master)](https://travis-ci.org/sindresorhus/path-exists)"
.PP
.RS 4
Check if a path exists 
.RE
.PP

.PP
NOTE: \fRfs\&.existsSync\fP has been un-deprecated in Node\&.js since 6\&.8\&.0\&. If you only need to check synchronously, this module is not needed\&.

.PP
While \fR\fRfs\&.exists()\fP\fP is being \fRdeprecated\fP, there's still a genuine use-case of being able to check if a path exists for other purposes than doing IO with it\&.

.PP
Never use this before handling a file though:

.PP
.RS 4
In particular, checking if a file exists before opening it is an anti-pattern that leaves you vulnerable to race conditions: another process may remove the file between the calls to \fRfs\&.exists()\fP and \fRfs\&.open()\fP\&. Just open the file and handle the error when it's not there\&. 
.RE
.PP
.SH "Install"
.PP
.PP
.nf
$ npm install path\-exists
.fi
.PP
.SH "Usage"
.PP
.PP
.nf
// foo\&.js
const pathExists = require('path\-exists');

(async () => {
    console\&.log(await pathExists('foo\&.js'));
    //=> true
})();
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
.SS "pathExists(path)"
Returns a \fRPromise<boolean>\fP of whether the path exists\&.
.SS "pathExists\&.sync(path)"
Returns a \fRboolean\fP of whether the path exists\&.
